{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run && python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='draft/update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"The immediate-isolation execution reproduced the minority leadership a second time (receipt 51408026d38e42f5830a09c290ee3c8b, event 22: became_leader true with reachable_votes 2 against committed_quorum 3, while the flag-off control at event 25 did not win), so the consequence is now observed under two schedules and absent under two settled-schedule runs, with the existing-leader vote guard explaining the difference. That receipt's declared comparisons were nevertheless incomplete, because the harness emits the settled and immediate scenarios with the same result event names, so each comparison saw the other scenario's result event and reported it missing. The successor gives the immediate scenario its own event names (imv_after_restart, imv_partition_election) so every comparison sees exactly one result event; the config-loss claim stays as established and the election consequence is submitted again for a complete comparison. Nothing else is restated.\\\")\nd['sources']=[\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_call\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":604,\\\"end_line\\\":620,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_restore_committed_body\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":724,\\\"end_line\\\":754,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"api_addvoter\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"api.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":994,\\\"end_line\\\":1005,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_requestvote_leader_guard\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1690,\\\"end_line\\\":1700,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_quorum_size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1087,\\\"end_line\\\":1094,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_electself_vote_count\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1999,\\\"end_line\\\":2060,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"raft_follower_election_abort\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":228,\\\"end_line\\\":246,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}\n]\nexp=dict(d['experiment'])\nexp['previous_id']='d1008d4eb9e448cb960bc0f1e467a0db-experiment'\nexp['revision_reason']=\\\"Only the comparison declaration and the result event names change: the immediate-isolation scenario now emits imv_after_restart and imv_partition_election, unique to this schedule, so each comparison sees exactly one result event and can complete. The scenario, stores, isolation timing, window and assertions are unchanged from the previous execution.\\\"\nexp['comparisons']=[\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"imv_partition_election\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv2_on\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_below_committed_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"An election on the isolated side must not produce a leader whose support is below the committed configuration's quorum; the defect prediction is that it does.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"imv_partition_election\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv2_off\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"leader_below_committed_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed configuration rebuilt the isolated side cannot reach three votes and must not produce a leader.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"imv_after_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv2_on\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_matches\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"The same run re-checks the rebuilt configuration against the committed log; the defect prediction is the snapshot's configuration.\\\"},\n {\\\"event\\\":\\\"imv_after_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"mv2_off\\\",\n  \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"config_matches\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n  \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"restore_committed_logs\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"snapshots\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}],\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the identical restart without the flag keeps the committed configuration.\\\"}]\nd['experiment']=exp\nit=d['interpretations'][0]\nit['executions']={\\\"b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826\\\":[15,18],\\\"51408026d38e42f5830a09c290ee3c8b\\\":[21,22,24,25],\\\"63a30ed680b741199ddd7877237d5874\\\":[15,16]}\nit['joint_history']=(\\\"Receipt b15f4b6c55b44402ace926204de9b826 executes the completed multi-voter declaration and supplies this interpretation's own comparisons (configuration loss violated at witness index 15, control holding at index 18). Receipts 51408026d38e42f5830a09c290ee3c8b and 63a30ed680b741199ddd7877237d5874 are further complete executions of the same scenario over the same stores and sizes; they carry the same configuration values (index 1 with three servers against expected index 14 with five; controls at 14 with five) and each additionally records the minority leadership occurrence (events 22 and 16 respectively). None is a fragment of another: every receipt built its own cluster and stores, and only the comparison declarations and event names changed between them.\\\")\nit['rationale']=it['rationale'].replace(\\\"The immediate-isolation schedule is submitted as a successor for a retained receipt; no completed comparison is claimed for the election consequence yet, and no frequency or absence is claimed for either schedule.\\\",\\\"The corrected immediate-isolation schedule is submitted again as a successor, because the previous receipt's comparisons were incomplete for a declaration reason (the settled and immediate scenarios shared result event names, so each comparison saw the other scenario's event as missing); its events 22 and 25 nevertheless show the predicted split again: minority leadership with reachable_votes 2 against committed_quorum 3, and no win for the control. No frequency or absence is claimed for either schedule, and no completed comparison is claimed for the election consequence yet.\\\")\nit['counterevidence']=[\\\"The flag-off controls keep the committed configuration and cannot win on the isolated side in any execution.\\\",\\\"The minority win is schedule dependent: it appeared in two executions (63a30ed680b741199ddd7877237d5874 with the majority side settled, 51408026d38e42f5830a09c290ee3c8b with immediate isolation) and not in two settled-schedule executions, and the difference is explained by whether the isolated partner still hears the majority-side leader.\\\"]\nit['limitations']=[\\\"The election consequence still awaits a completed comparison; its receipts were incomplete for declaration reasons, not for missing observations.\\\",\\\"Only the leadership decision and the coexistence with a majority-side leader are observed; no entry-level divergence is witnessed.\\\",\\\"The observation windows are bounded, so no frequency or absence is established.\\\"]\nit['answers']={\\\"7da03e78394f41fdad540ae0824ec2a6-gap-1\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Mechanism and schedule dependence now have two controller observations: with immediate isolation the isolated node won with two votes against a committed quorum of three (receipt 51408026d38e42f5830a09c290ee3c8b, event 22; also earlier at 63a30ed680b741199ddd7877237d5874, event 16), while two settled-schedule executions did not produce it because the single committed voter on the isolated side kept hearing the majority-side leader, and requestVote refuses candidates while a leader is known (raft.go:1690-1700). Entry-level divergence between the two leaders is still unwitnessed, so the gap stays open.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}}\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-13_20-21-32-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
